# keytrack, filter sweep depth in OCTAVES — the "after" half of audit §B2b (plan 2.1b).
# Presses 3 (keytrack 1.00, so the BASE cutoff already follows the note) then 6 (ENV_CUTOFF_OCT, depth in octaves).
#
# WHY THE 3 FIRST, and it is load-bearing: with tracking off, base and sweep-top are both flat and the two
# units sound and look IDENTICAL. The Hz form only exposes itself once the base moves — so a seed that
# skipped the 3 would render an A/B that proves nothing.
#
# The cart SELF-PLAYS on boot (running = true), so the four-octave phrase runs with an otherwise empty
# script. This pair is the EAR check: the sweep is fat down low and gone up top, the twin of 01, where it holds its size at every pitch.
# It is NOT the ruler — the phrase gates 420 ms notes every 200 ms, so notes OVERLAP and a per-note
# spectral region is polluted by the two before it (measured: non-monotonic, and the two modes read the
# same at the first C). The acceptance numbers come from the isolated-note probe recorded in
# docs/design/synth-secrets-plan.md §2.1(b), not from here.
down 10 3
up 13 3
down 20 6
up 23 6
